    public void processRequest(byte[] serializedData) {
        // DANGEROUS: Deserializing untrusted input
        ObjectInputStream ois = new ObjectInputStream(
            new ByteArrayInputStream(serializedData)
        );
        Object obj = ois.readObject(); // Security risk!
    }
}
```

### Defensive Measures

**1. Avoid Deserialization of Untrusted Data**
```java
// SECURE: Use safe alternatives
public class SecureEndpoint {
    public void processRequest(String jsonData) {
        // Use JSON instead of Java serialization
        ObjectMapper mapper = new ObjectMapper();
        MyData obj = mapper.readValue(jsonData, MyData.class);
    }
}
```

**2. Implement Deserialization Allowlists**
```java
// SECURE: Validate classes before deserialization
public class SafeObjectInputStream extends ObjectInputStream {
    private final List<String> allowedClasses;

    @Override
    protected Class<?> resolveClass(ObjectStreamClass desc) {
        if (!allowedClasses.contains(desc.getName())) {
            throw new SecurityException("Unauthorized class");
        }
        return super.resolveClass(desc);
    }
}
```

